{
  "comment": "The web client's routes (cmuxterm-hq docs/rfd/0083-cmux-web-client.md, Deeplinks), so the Rust reader and the web host cannot drift. Forms: /m/<machine>/agent/<harness>/<session>[?message=<id>], /m/<machine>/ws/<ws_ id>, /deeplink/agent?<agent link query> (schemas/deeplinks/agent-link.json), and a whole pasted cmux://agent, cmux://workspace or https://cmux.com/deeplink/agent link. <machine> is machine_<32 hex> (route.machine.id) or a machine name (route.machine.name). Of a query only message is read: a repeated, empty or malformed one names nothing. A link is an address and never runs anything. Readers: cmux-tui/crates/cmux-web-route/src/route.rs (every vector) and webviews/src/web-host/route.ts (the vectors whose address is a path, starting with /). error is RouteError::code; path is the route's canonical web path, which reads back to the same route.",
  "vectors": [
    {"name": "agent by machine name", "address": "/m/my-vm/agent/claude/01a16c8c-54ec-71b2-a0fa-125d1404dd72", "route": {"kind": "agent", "machine": {"name": "my-vm"}, "harness": "claude", "session": "01a16c8c-54ec-71b2-a0fa-125d1404dd72"}, "path": "/m/my-vm/agent/claude/01a16c8c-54ec-71b2-a0fa-125d1404dd72"},
    {"name": "agent by machine id, with a message", "address": "/m/machine_0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef/agent/codex/s:1?message=m-42", "route": {"kind": "agent", "machine": {"id": "machine_0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"}, "harness": "codex", "session": "s:1", "message": "m-42"}, "path": "/m/machine_0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef/agent/codex/s:1?message=m-42"},
    {"name": "a trailing slash and an escaped colon read the same", "address": "/m/my-vm/agent/codex/s%3A1/", "route": {"kind": "agent", "machine": {"name": "my-vm"}, "harness": "codex", "session": "s:1"}, "path": "/m/my-vm/agent/codex/s:1"},
